cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Tessera: reference-anchored detection of recombination in viral genomes"
message: "If you use Tessera in work you publish, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "FOI Bioinformatics"
    website: "https://github.com/FOI-Bioinformatics"
repository-code: "https://github.com/FOI-Bioinformatics/tessera"
license: MIT
version: 1.1.0
abstract: >-
  Tessera detects recombination in a query genome against a reference panel. It builds a
  reference-anchored pseudo-MSA, scans it in sliding windows, and calls recombinant
  regions with an ensemble of complementary methods: an HMM segmentation caller, a
  scan-aware 3SEQ triplet test, MaxChi, and Bootscan, alongside a parent-free PHI/Rmin
  diagnostic that fires even when the true donor is absent from the panel. It is an
  indicative screen rather than a full phylogenetic test; strong candidates should be
  confirmed with a dedicated method.
keywords:
  - bioinformatics
  - recombination
  - virus
  - genomics
  - phylogenetics
